<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chen Li (Chen Han)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chen Li was the son and heir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-youliang">Chen Youliang</a>, the rebel who founded the Chen Han state in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. After his father was killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a>'s forces at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lake-poyang">Battle of Lake Poyang</a> in 1363, Chen Li succeeded him but surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuchang">Wuchang</a> in 1364. His lands passed to Zhu, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> four years later.</p></div>
